      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: s/sentitve/sensitive/\n\nAnd another nit: this explanation seems a bit too narrowed: those pages may be also donated to the hypervisor, not just to a pVM, and those stale entries may also allow the host, for example, to modify the hypervisor\u0027s code (which is obviously just as bad, or even worse, than reading pVM\u0027s sensitive data).\n\npKVM must always protect pVM-owned and hypervisor-owned pages from access by the host, that\u0027s pKVM\u0027s job, we don\u0027t need to explain why pKVM needs to do that. :) \n\nSo we could reword this a bit e.g. like: \"...Unmapped pages may be donated to a pVM or to the hypervisor. Until a flush happens, stale entries in cache could enable a device to access those pages, breaking pKVM security guarantees. So perform flush immediately.\"",
      "revId": "c5fcb114d6350e4b9a05794a1575ab506a92532b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
